* Capacitively shunted flux qubit (CSFQ).
*
* A loop of three junctions, one smaller by ALPHA, with a large capacitor across the
* small one. Away from half flux it is a transmon: high frequency, negative
* anharmonicity. Near half flux the quadratic part of the potential nearly cancels,
* the quartic part takes over, and the anharmonicity turns strongly positive.

.title  Capacitively shunted flux qubit
.name   csfq

.param  EJ0   = 80.0            ; GHz, the two large junctions
.param  ALPHA = 0.43            ; the third junction is ALPHA times smaller

J1  0  1  EJ=EJ0          EC=4.0
J2  1  2  EJ=EJ0          EC=4.0
J3  2  0  EJ={EJ0*ALPHA}  EC={4.0/ALPHA}
Csh 2  0  EC=0.30               ; the shunt

.flux   1 = 0.5
.cutoff all = 12
.levels 5
.end
